      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-72449: integrating each term gives half its logarithm; combining logarithms gives the selected product expression, with C=(1/2)ln K for K>0, on intervals excluding x=±1/2. q-13944: the diagram gives adjacent vectors (3,2) and (2,-2), so the area is |3(-2)-2(2)|=10. q-13951: the area is |1(3)-5(-4)|=23. q-69943: the vectors are parallel and their determinant is 4(1/2)-6(1/3)=0. q-70868: the diameter midpoint is ((0+8)/2,(2+4)/2)=(4,3). q-115360: the diameter has length 3, so the radius is 3/2. q-45759: the diameter has length sqrt(4²+(-2)²)=2sqrt(5), so the radius is sqrt(5). q-115364: the diameter midpoint is (0,3), and its distance to (-1,2) is sqrt(2). q-54202: x²+y²=169 has center (0,0) and radius sqrt(169)=13. q-7463 and q-7513: the graphs show circles centered at the origin with radii 3 and 8, respectively, giving right sides 9 and 64. q-71506: distance 5 from the origin means x²+y²=25. q-14793 and q-116927: the given endpoints have squared distances 34 and 5 from the origin, respectively. q-70896: center (1,2) and radius 5 give (x-1)²+(y-2)²=25. q-117081: center (-5,0) and radius 7 give (x+5)²+y²=49. No earlier submitted answers or revealed grades were supplied; confirmation uses the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
